<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The restart dialog (uirestart.py RestartDialog, uiscript
	     restartdialog.py): shown when the main character dies, closed by the
	     server's CloseRestartWindow when a restart succeeds. While the
	     restart flag is on, the Interface makes the facade
	     nui_restart.RestartDialog (controller assets/root/nui_restart.py).
	     The document exists only while the dialog shows (nui_hud.OnDemand).
	     Restart here and Restart in the city send legacy's commands and leave
	     the dialog open: the server refuses them for its first seconds and
	     says so in an info line. Escape and the exit key are kept and do
	     nothing, as legacy's (nui_hud.EscapeProxy). The body and its buttons
	     take no focus, so the buttons act on a left mousedown. -->
	<title>restart</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="restart.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="nui-window nui-anim restart" data-model="restart">
	<div class="restart__buttons">
		<button id="restart-here" class="nui-button nui-anim restart__button restart__button--here" data-event-mousedown="act('here', ev.button)">@ui.RESTART_HERE</button>
		<button id="restart-town" class="nui-button nui-anim restart__button restart__button--town" data-event-mousedown="act('town', ev.button)">@ui.RESTART_TOWN</button>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
